WEBVTT

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.980
You're here to grant my wish?

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:08.900
Yup!

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.190
Noel,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.240
seven years ago...

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.450
Yes?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.330
No, I just—

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.500
Nonoka?!

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.590
It can't be, can it?

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.890
Here you go, Nonoka!

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.640
Thank you, Noel.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.820
The weather's nice...

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.180
Good morning, Dad.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.510
Mornin'.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.310
Are two eggs okay with you?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.350
Yeah.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.640
Sunny-side up?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:25.690
Whatever you want.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.860
Should you still be in your pajamas?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.740
Speak for yourself, Dad.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.740
Well, it's fine as long as you make it on time.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.740
In time for what?

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.240
School.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:42.910
Huh?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.000
The opening ceremony's today, isn't it?

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.170
What?

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.420
But it's only August—

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.250
Yeah, I guess it's earlier
than the schools in Tokyo.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.430
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.930
Well, it's the same as when you went to
elementary school here, so I figured you'd know.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.970
I can't remember something from that long ago!

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.400
Toast the bread for me!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.480
Sure thing.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.030
Dad,

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.740
you moron!

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.160
I'm Komiya Nonoka.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.330
Pleased to meet all of you.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.170
Maybe you should try smiling a bit more.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.640
Those eggs are probably overcooked now.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.550
Hey, you were the one
who let me decide!

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.390
Take care on the way, okay?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.850
See you later!

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:54.860
Nonoka!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.570
Noel!

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.030
I came to see you.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.740
Sorry, Noel! I'm in a hurry!

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.450
It's all my Dad's fault!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.460
See you again later!

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.790
Bye.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.690
Welcome.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.440
Did you find the girl you were looking for?

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.950
Oh, so you weren't a tourist.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.690
No, but it hasn't been
very long since I moved here.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.950
Do you know which class
you're going to be in?

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.830
No, not yet.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:51.000
There aren't many people from this town who go to our school.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:51.870
Really?

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.330
Yup.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.800
It'd be lovely if we're in the same class.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.840
Yes, it would.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.630
I'm Komiya Nonoka.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.050
Pleased to meet all of you.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.430
Okay, class, let's all be sure
to make her feel welcome.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.940
You'll be sitting at the end
of row two, Komiya-san.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:22.820
Um...

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.820
Um!

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.540
Don't you dare touch me.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.420
You could have just answered if you'd heard me.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.830
Why should I?

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:40.630
Huh?

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:47.470
We met before by the lake, didn't we?

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.600
And?

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.060
I was curious why you said that to me.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.700
I wonder if there's anything fun to do.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:23.840
When will Nonoka be back?

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.470
Komiya-san, let's go home together.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.090
You can just call me Nonoka.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.560
Just Koharu is fine for me, too.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.190
Is your house near the lake?

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:35.810
Yup.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:39.730
It's closer to the mountains though, so it's a little far to the lake.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:41.730
This mornin—

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.780
Hold it!

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.360
Um...

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.240
That's Mizusaka Yuzuki.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:51.650
You!

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.410
Is what you said true?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.250
Huh?

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:58.250
I asked, did you really move to Kiriyako?

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.340
Yes... I did.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:04.460
Come with me.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.330
Huh?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.220
W-Wait!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.430
Just come on!

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.150
Wait a second, Mizusaka-san!

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.360
What do you want with me?

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.480
Tell me exactly how you feel.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:30.730
Feel about what?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.610
What else?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:34.660
Do you like it?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.160
Huh?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.080
Or don't you?!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:36.750
Huh?

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.500
I'm talking about the Disc!

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:45.830
Hey, could we get two ginger ales, please?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.930
You don't mind having the same thing, do you?

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:49.630
No...

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.220
I don't really mind.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.810
Er... so where were we?

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:57.350
There's more?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.520
Of course there is!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.400
It's a big deal, okay?!

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.480
Calm down, please?

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:10.320
I don't know if you're aware,
but it was a huge issue seven years back.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.450
It was on the news, so I know a little bit.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.620
Also, right about then I was—

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.530
It's not the same unless you were actually here!

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.670
The Disc appeared out of nowhere

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.040
and it's just stayed above the lake since then,

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.620
but no one seems to care at all now!

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:30.130
All right, I hear you.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.180
Sit down. Our drinks are here.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.810
And besides, because of that Disc—

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.440
You can have mine too!

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:56.610
The rest of the townspeople don't seem to mind, though.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.620
They're all being fooled.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:00.120
By whom?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.490
By the Disc!

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:03.830
Isn't that obvious?!

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:10.260
It's just been sitting there for the past seven years,

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.680
but we don't know what it could be hiding!

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:19.010
The safety of this town is being
jeopardized day after day!

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:22.690
We have to do something before it's too late!

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:25.650
This town seems to be the epitome of safe, though...

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.820
Who are you siding with exactly, Nonoka?

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:29.990
Your friend who needs your help, or that Disc?!

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.990
Well, my friend who needs my help, I guess.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.990
Then it's settled!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.290
We'll bring back peace to this town!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.580
Just the two of us!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.960
We need your help!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.210
Please help...

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.670
Let's take back our town!

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.790
...take back our town.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.210
Please help!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.330
Please help out!

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.170
Come on, you too, Nonoka.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.800
Don't call out my name!

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.010
You've gotta be louder!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.340
Otherwise, no one will hear you.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:06.090
No, I meant—

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:07.430
Oh, I know!

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.310
Wanna use this?

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:15.480
No thanks!

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.980
I'll be fine.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:17.940
You sure?

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.200
Please help us!

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.700
Let's drive that Disc away from our town!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.370
We have no need for that Disc in our town!

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:33.910
We mustn't slow down
in our efforts to drive it away!

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:35.410
What's up?

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.000
Oh, sorry.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.340
How much longer are we going to be doing this?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.380
Until the Disc goes away.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:42.880
Are you serious?

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.460
'Course I am!

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:48.720
It'll be a piece of cake with everyone's support!

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:55.770
Koharu...

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.480
What are you doing,

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.520
dear customers?

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.780
This is, um...

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:04.570
Right?

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.610
We're, uh, doing our civic duty...

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.240
I think we should apologize!

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.160
Time for plan B!

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:14.950
B?

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.430
Why'd you run away?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.140
Because!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:38.520
We didn't do anything wrong.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.400
Then we should have just explained to her...

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.810
Fat chance.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.820
I've known her for too long.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.150
I know exactly how she'd react.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.530
Thanks, Nonoka.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:52.700
Huh?

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.870
Thanks for coming here with me.

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.790
Well, things just turned out this way.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.250
Still! It made me feel happy,

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:02.790
so thanks for that.

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:04.630
Sure...

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.760
Ok! Time for plan C!

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.340
There's a C?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.510
Thanks for waiting.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.800
Do you have an inquiry about the Disc?

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:15.760
Yes!

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.480
In that case, could you please fill out this form?

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:24.860
Thanks, but I'd prefer to speak directly to whoever's in charge.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.820
Who's the boss around here? I want to—

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:27.820
We're so sorry!

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.400
Never mind!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.860
Let go of me, Nonoka!

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:33.990
I have to speak with the boss!

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.080
The boss!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.370
Lemme see the boss!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.290
Why'd you stop me?

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:46.710
You wouldn't have been able to speak to them anyway.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.630
You can't say that for sure.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.300
We used to be able to go on cruises to that island in the past, you know,

00:13:57.930 --> 00:14:02.230
but since then, it's been closed off because it's "too dangerous".

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:05.730
That doesn't make any sense to me.

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.480
I won't accept how things are right now.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:14.200
We have to take back our town.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.080
Sorry she's such a bother for you.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:29.380
Don't be mad at Yuzuki.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:32.170
I understand how she feels.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:40.350
Where'd I put it?

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.140
What are you looking for?

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.140
A weapon.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.300
Nonoka!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.420
I finally found it!

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:19.390
Righty, we're all set!

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.100
What do you think you're doing?

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.980
Why should I tell you?

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.400
Sorry for intruding.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.280
Mind telling me what that's about?

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.820
That's none of your business either.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:42.700
Stop going around making things
difficult for other people.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:46.000
I bet it's something stupid anyway.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.000
It's not stupid.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.460
Why do you insist on keeping this up?

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.130
"Why?"

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.340
I knew it.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:15:59.680
Yuzuki?

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.140
I knew it!

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.350
Everything is the Disc and that girl's fault!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:10.650
What's up with her?

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.560
Um...

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:12.860
Sorry for bothering you!

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.620
Wait, new girl.

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.740
Maybe it's better you don't.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:38.170
Souta, you idiot!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.470
Stupid Souta!

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:40.840
Stupid, stupid...

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:43.350
What are you doing?

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:45.970
Resorting to drastic measures.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.480
I'm going to get to that island.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:49.940
You can't!

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:50.980
That's too—

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.730
Unless I do this,

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:57.070
I won't be able to change anything.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.120
Take my backpack.

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.410
Let's go, Nonoka.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.340
Fine. I'll just go by myself.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:24.180
I've been alone this whole time, anyway.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.100
Mizusaka-san!

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:45.910
You're angry, aren't you?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.700
No, not really.

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.120
I'm sorry.

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.170
Can I ask you something?

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:57.670
Yeah.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:06.010
Why do you want to get rid of the Disc so badly?

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:16.520
There are some things that changed
when the Disc appeared seven years ago.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.610
Some things that haven't changed back even now.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:27.280
During the summer festival,
fireworks were lit above the lake.

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:28.870
Fireworks?

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.160
It wasn't a massive display or anything,

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:37.090
but the sight of the fireworks reflected on the water's surface was beautiful.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.960
But now...

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.800
they don't do them anymore.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:01.440
Let's fire it.

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:05.780
This flies, right?

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:09.080
Let's fire the rocket.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:11.580
Sure.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:15.160
Three, two, one!

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.010
Go!

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:37.520
It hardly got anywhere.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:39.860
Yuzuki.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:42.940
I'll help you.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.360
Let's do something about that Disc together.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:47.450
Will you really?

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:49.160
Yup.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.030
As long as it's safe, of course.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.040
Really?

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:55.120
Really.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:59.290
We'll need to find more people to help us.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.340
Nonoka.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.260
Thanks.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:31.030
It's pretty!

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.950
I wish Dad had come, too.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:37.710
Yes, he should have.

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.380
Nonoka, have you been keeping
that promise you made with me?

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.130
Yup, I have!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:51.010
Of course! That's my baby girl.

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:54.970
Mom, I...

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:56.850
Nonoka.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:01.060
Nonoka, what's wrong?

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.400
Are you feeling bad?

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:04.900
Noel.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.320
What's bothering you?

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.030
Is it something Noel can help you with?

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.910
Will you help us too, Noel?

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.040
Count me in!

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:23.080
What do you want Noel to do?

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:26.960
We're trying to get rid of the Disc from this town.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:32.180
Nonoka, you don't like the Disc?

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:38.480
It's not that, but I want to
do something to help my friend.

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:40.730
Okay then.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.060
Just wait a little bit, okay?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.190
Great!

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:49.150
This makes three of us now.

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:34.180
Next time, on Sora no Method:

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.760
"The Memory's Whereabouts."

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:37.010
Look forward to it!
